-# Cooperative input projection probe
+# Cooperative input projection probe at macOS 26.2
 
 This is one source-only experiment. It has not been compiled or run. It changes no product files and loads only three existing Flash projection matrices, not a complete model.
+
+
+This follow-on preserves the earlier probe's baseline, candidate, Swift host,
+fixtures, oracles, timing schedule, and acceptance gates byte for byte. The only
+shader build change is adding `-mmacosx-version-min=26.2` to **both** baseline and
+candidate compilation. The earlier default target was measured as 26.0, selecting
+destination-only SDK helpers for input tensors. The separate
+[coordinate proof](../register-target26_2-diagnostic/publication-v1/README.md)
+confirmed that the fixed 26.2 target restores exact input coordinates and bits
+without a mapping edit. That proof did not execute a GEMM.
+
+`source-delta.json` records every unchanged and changed source hash, and
+`source-changes.patch` records the wrapper/metadata changes. The guard now pins
+the reviewed source and current shared guard hashes, records SDK header identity,
+checks the supporting coordinate proof, and fails if its monitor reports an error
+during cleanup. No bound is raised. The build refuses to overwrite an earlier
+attempt. This is one fixed bench attempt after review and an explicit handoff;
+no separate check run or retry is authorized by this document.
+
+Production runtime compilation remains unverified by this offline experiment.
+Even a successful GEMM result would need separate runtime-compilation and complete
+weighted-model acceptance before integration.
 
 ## Fixed candidate
 
